<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prithvipati I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 885</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prithvipati I was a prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ganga-dynasty">Western Ganga dynasty</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> and an ally of the Pallavas in their wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>. He joined the Pallava king Aparajita at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sripurambiyam">Battle of Sripurambiyam</a> around 885, where the Pandya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varaguna-ii">Varaguna II</a> was defeated, but was killed in the battle.</p></div>
